---
description: Agent Bridge debugging discipline
globs:
alwaysApply: false
---

When debugging a full-stack issue with multiple agents:

- use the Agent Bridge MCP as the source of truth for cross-agent communication
- keep frontend and backend responsibilities separate
- every meaningful conclusion must include evidence
- every question must be narrow and answerable
- separate facts, hypotheses, and unknowns
- prefer eliminating one hypothesis before creating a new one
- do not mark a case resolved until root cause, fix, and validation steps are explicit

Preferred bug buckets:
- route mismatch
- schema mismatch
- auth/session issue
- CORS / headers / CSRF
- environment/config drift
- async timing / race
- stale contract drift
- serialization bug
- backend exception
- upstream dependency failure
- cache inconsistency
- optimistic UI masking real failure
